Day 21: Generative AI using LangChain

What is LangChain:
Open source framework. You can make any application based on an LLM. That is an LLM based application.

Build complex AI such as chatbot, Q and A system, RAG, agents, etc.

LangChain has support for all major LLMs. That is one of its most important features.

It simplifies developing LLM based applications.

We get different integrations in LangChain. We have wrappers to connect with services.

It is free and open source.

Supports all major Gen AI use cases.

Why LangChain first for user side perspective:
From LangChain we can work with both open source, closed source, LLM APIs, Hugging Face, Llama, etc.

LangChain has 3 parts:
1. LangChain fundamentals (most important part)
2. RAG applications
3. AI agents

Embedding = convert the whole document into vectors that are numbers.

We do not only convert the PDF into embedding. We also convert the query into a vector.

Chunking can be done based on pages, paragraph, chapter, or anything.

PDF -> embedding -> database
User query -> embedding -> semantic search -> database
System prompt (pages + user query) -> LLM -> output

LangChain helps us handle moving parts like changing the LLM API, for example using Gemini instead of ChatGPT.

Benefits:
1. Concepts of chains. Helps in chain pipeline.
2. Easily reusable, removable, addable.
3. Complete ecosystem.
4. Has memory concepts.

What can we build:
1. Chatbot
2. AI knowledge assistant
3. AI agents
4. Workflow automation
5. Research helper

